    "expensive_path": "the user source terms of the ionospheric chemistry: per-cell photoionization, charge exchange, recombination and ion-neutral collision rates from neutral-atmosphere profiles (Mars, Venus, Titan) evaluated every step and updated point-implicitly, on a spherical stretched grid around the body; the giant-planet and Mercury cases add rotating-frame and layered inner-boundary sources",
    "rationale": "each planet has its own user module and equation set, but they are one family: unmagnetised or weakly magnetised bodies with a chemically active ionosphere as the inner boundary, and the same test recipe (short steady-state run, restart save and read, log-file comparison)",
    "excluded": [
      "Earth (geospace module)",
      "comets (cometary module)",
      "Ganymede and Europa (srcUserExtra)"
    ],
    "hazards": [
      "five of the tests include a restart-save and restart-read half, comparing that the restarted log continues the original",
      "the runs are steady-state iterations with a fixed MaxIteration compared by log files at very tight absolute tolerances (1e-15 to 1e-17)",
      "Mercury reads a layered-conductivity inner boundary and Saturn a three-species set; some need util/DATAREAD readers"
    ]
  },
